-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/4d0b1a7f-7fcd-4504-9b7e-d76320e2ffe1
-- title:
--   Regularity and DEC of the original data in a collar source patch
-- statement:
--   Let $P$ be a collar source patch for spatial tensors $A,B$ and $S>0$. Assume that outside radius $S$, the fields $A,B$ are $C^\infty$ and symmetric, the metric `sourceSpatial A` is positive definite and `spatialDEC (sourceSpatial A) (sourceSpatial B)` holds, and assume that the leading coefficients $m^r,m^g,m^K$ of $P$ are $C^\infty$ on its region. Then at every point $y$ of the tail region of $P$ above $S$, the fields of $P$ are smooth, the source metric is positive definite, the tangential source tensor is symmetric, and the source data satisfy `physicalDEC` with the source frame.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In the scope of the preamble:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem original_source_patch_properties {A B : SpatialTensor} (P : CollarSourcePatch A B)
--       {S : ℝ} (hS : 0 < S)
--       (hAs : ∀ x, S < ‖x‖ → ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ A x)
--       (hBs : ∀ x, S < ‖x‖ → ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ B x)
--       (hA : ∀ x, S < ‖x‖ → ∀ v w, A x v w = A x w v)
--       (hB : ∀ x, S < ‖x‖ → ∀ v w, B x v w = B x w v)
--       (hpos : ∀ x, S < ‖x‖ → ∀ v : E, v ≠ 0 → 0 < sourceSpatial A x v v)
--       (hDEC : ∀ x, S < ‖x‖ → spatialDEC (sourceSpatial A) (sourceSpatial B) x)
--       (hmr : ∀ θ ∈ P.region, ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ P.mr θ)
--       (hmg : ∀ a b θ, θ ∈ P.region → ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ (P.mg a b) θ)
--       (hmK : ∀ a b θ, θ ∈ P.region → ContDiffAt ℝ ∞ (P.mK a b) θ)
--       {y : CKSMixedGeometry.Point} (hy : y ∈ angularRadialTail S P.region) :
--       P.fields.SmoothAt y ∧ (sourceMetric P.fields.base y).PosDef ∧
--       (sourceTangentialK P.fields.base y).IsHermitian ∧
--       physicalDEC (sourceMetric P.fields.base) (sourceTensor P.fields)
--         (sourceFrame P.fields.base) y
--   ```
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is verbatim from `lean/OAI/Geometry/Relativity/CKS/TailEnergy.lean`, lines 3813-3873, in OpenAI's `openai/math` at commit `adc7f12` (Apache-2.0), formalizing part of the construction in the preprint *Area-controlled end replacement and the Bondi–Penrose inequality in the CKS class* (OpenAI, September 27, 2026). It is a supporting lemma for `OAI.CKSSourceExterior.area_controlled_end_replacement`. The definitions it mentions are those of `Definitions.Def_CKSBondiPenrose` and `Definitions.Def_CKSEndReplacementSupport`.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/lean/OAI/Geometry/Relativity/CKS/TailEnergy.lean#L3813-L3873 ; preprint preprints/Area-controlled-end-replacement-and-the-Bondi-Penrose-inequality-in-the-CKS-class-September-27-2026/paper.pdf in the same repository

